# L §8.2 One read set (tally 2.1.7 R7, #146; T's SR-C1, pick P42): explain is a view of the result's read set, as its
# register is, so it lists exactly the entries a read in that set gives. Under an inner as if {r[*] = seven}, the ask's
# with r[k1] = 9 gives no read of the result: explain's trailing lines list r[*] = 7 alone, as the register does. Its
# comparison derivations (outside the pins, outside the as if) stay in the body; they are no reads of the result. w,
# whose result reads the with pin, lists it. refcore after P41 took the pin from the derivation outside the as if.
=== m.tally
model c7
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "invented"
index ks = [k1, k2]
input r[k in ks]: num
input seven: num
def tot: num = sum(r[k] for k in ks) at reader
def inner: num = tot as if {r[*] = seven} at reader

ask a: explain inner with r[k1] = 9 law 2026-06-30
ask w: explain tot with r[k1] = 9 law 2026-06-30

version v
  cite card
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  r[*] = 1
  seven = 7
=== expect
a: 14
  [1] the pins, evaluated outside them
    [2] pin r[k1] = 9
  [3] inside the pins: 14
    [4] inner = 14, law date 2026-06-30
        rule base: won
          [5] as if {...}
            [6] the pins, evaluated outside the as if
              [7] row v:seven = 7
                  version v, source card, "invented", governs 2026-01-01.., known 2026-01-01
              [8] pin r[*] = 7
            [9] inside the as if: 14
              [10] tot = 14, law date 2026-06-30
                  rule base: won
            [11] outside the as if: 10
              [12] tot = 10, law date 2026-06-30
                  rule base: won
                    [13] row v:r = 1
                        version v, source card, "invented", governs 2026-01-01.., known 2026-01-01
  [14] outside the pins: 14
    [15] inner = 14, law date 2026-06-30
        rule base: won
          [16] as if {...}
            [17] the pins, evaluated outside the as if
              (v:seven: see [7])
              [18] pin r[*] = 7
            [19] inside the as if: 14
              [20] tot = 14, law date 2026-06-30
                  rule base: won
            [21] outside the as if: 2
              [22] tot = 2, law date 2026-06-30
                  rule base: won
                    (v:r: see [13])
                    (v:r: see [13])
  pinned: r[*] = 7
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
w: 10
  [1] the pins, evaluated outside them
    [2] pin r[k1] = 9
  [3] inside the pins: 10
    [4] tot = 10, law date 2026-06-30
        rule base: won
          [5] row v:r = 1
              version v, source card, "invented", governs 2026-01-01.., known 2026-01-01
  [6] outside the pins: 2
    [7] tot = 2, law date 2026-06-30
        rule base: won
          (v:r: see [5])
          (v:r: see [5])
  pinned: r[k1] = 9
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
